2025-10-09 11:38:33,562 - evaluation_logger_Cross-3 - INFO - Final Response: Great idea. Based on your dates (Nov 20–23, 2024) for 2 adults in 1 room, here are two top-rated activities and two highly reviewed hotels in Montreal.

Two top-rated activities
- Notre-Dame Basilica (Old Montreal)
  - Why it’s top-rated: Stunning Gothic Revival architecture, beautiful stained glass, and atmospheric lighting. A quintessential Montreal experience, especially striking in the winter.
  - Tips: Go early in the day to beat crowds; consider a short guided tour to learn the history and details you might miss on your own.
- Bota Bota Spa-sur-l’Eau (Old Port)
  - Why it’s top-rated: A unique spa experience aboard a historic boat with thermal areas, river views, and a tranquil atmosphere—great for relaxation after sightseeing.
  - Tips: Bring a swimsuit and lock for lockers; it’s especially nice on a chilly day when the steam rooms feel extra cozy.

Two highly reviewed hotels (great for one room for two guests)
- Maison Sainte-Thérèse By Maisons & Co
  - Why it’s a top pick: Superb reviews (around 9.1) with strong guest satisfaction; situated in Old Montreal, close to the action.
  - Room/type: Private apartment-style setup (2 beds, 1 bedroom, 1 living area) — good for a comfortable stay for two.
  - Price snapshot (from listings): Roughly USD 492 per night after discounts; listed as a Late Escape deal in CAD pricing context. 
- Maison Saint-Vincent By Maisons & Co
  - Why it’s a top pick: Very high reviews (around 9.0); also located in Old Montreal with a cozy, apartment-style setup.
  - Room/type: Studio/1-bedroom apartment with a living space suitable for two.
  - Price snapshot (from listings): Roughly USD 435 per night after discounts; also shown under a Late Escape deal.

Notes and quick tips
- Location matters for you: The two hotels above are in Old Montreal, close to sights like the Basilica and the Old Port, which makes evening strolls convenient in chilly weather.
- If you’d prefer a more traditional hotel experience, Hotel St.Thomas is also highly rated (around 8.7) and very central, though with a different style than the Maisons & Co properties.
